WEBVTT

00:00.040 --> 00:02.140
The topic of food can become

00:02.140 --> 00:04.196
overwhelming at times , and a lot of

00:04.196 --> 00:06.307
what we want to do is break that down

00:06.307 --> 00:08.473
into its simplest components . We have

00:08.473 --> 00:10.418
our good , better and best choices

00:10.418 --> 00:12.584
really across the board . So if you're

00:12.584 --> 00:14.640
looking down at your plate , is this

00:14.640 --> 00:16.862
something that you picked off a tree or

00:16.862 --> 00:18.751
dug up off the ground ? Those are

00:18.751 --> 00:20.807
really the kinds of foods that we're

00:20.807 --> 00:22.807
trying to aim for . This could also

00:22.807 --> 00:25.029
include things like nuts and seeds , as

00:25.029 --> 00:27.029
well as our fruits , vegetables and

00:27.029 --> 00:28.918
whole grains don't overcomplicate

00:28.918 --> 00:31.029
things from the vegetable side of the

00:31.029 --> 00:33.251
house , whether they're fresh frozen or

00:33.251 --> 00:35.418
canned , it could care less . I'm just

00:35.418 --> 00:37.751
happy that you're consuming a vegetable .

00:37.751 --> 00:37.540
Yeah .

